  "readback-solve-straight-limbs": {
    "reason": "A solve after the job read the pose back on the rig's root scaled by 100 (bone.rotateThenSolve, bone.solveTwice) works on the re-based skeleton, as the Editor's does: the body is displaced toward the root (bodyPosition z from -105.5 to -1.07 at step 0, alike in both) and the goals are out of reach, so the left arm is straight (forearm stretch muscle 1.06). The roll of a straight arm is one turn that the upper arm and forearm roll muscles (41, 43) split between them: Unbound's split is off the Editor's in steps of 1.8e-3 that cancel in their sum, with the upper arm's and hand's local rotations that follow. Consistent with amplified single-precision rounding: moving the goal by one single-precision step moves Unbound's own split by 5.4e-3 at step 16 (measured once); which steps differ depends on the host (macOS and Linux runs differ). The left foot's muscles 26 and 27 are off by up to 1.4e-3 on some steps, not traced further. The same solve before any read-back matches (bone.solve); see the residual row in docs/COMPATIBILITY_GAPS.md. Bounded instead of listed, so that a larger difference on any step fails: each of these muscles within 1e-2 (largest measured on macOS about 9.0e-3), the two roll muscles' sum within 1e-4 of the Editor's on every step (largest measured on macOS about 9.0e-5), and the upper arm's and hand's local rotations within 1e-2 per quaternion component (largest measured 3.7e-3); every other value keeps the comparator's tolerance.",
    "bounds": [
      {
        "key": "^bone\\.(rotateThenSolve|solveTwice)\\.step\\d+\\.pose$",
        "field": "^muscles\\[(26|27|41|43)\\]$",
        "within": 0.01
      },
      {
        "key": "^bone\\.(rotateThenSolve|solveTwice)\\.step\\d+\\.locals$",
        "field": "^Hips/Spine/Chest/UpperChest/LeftShoulder/LeftUpperArm(/LeftLowerArm/LeftHand)?\\[1\\]$",
        "within": 0.01
      }
    ],
    "sums": [
      {
        "key": "^bone\\.(rotateThenSolve|solveTwice)\\.step\\d+\\.pose$",
        "fields": [
          "muscles[41]",
          "muscles[43]"
        ],
        "within": 0.0001
      }
    ]
  }
}
